From d6c09b55b7780508de8fb2a15d5e5be81d4dd2b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taengu <7606218+taengu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:04:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Security: root checks the Linux update itself; Discord
 replies capped; CI pinned

From the 2026-10-26 security audit:
- A Linux update is copied into a folder only root can write, its SHA-256
  checked there and that copy installed, all in the one pkexec step: the
  download in the player's /tmp could be swapped after the meter checked
  it (M2).
- A Discord socket's reply longer than 1 MiB is refused before the crate
  allocates it (anything can create /tmp/discord-ipc-N or the pipe, and
  claim up to 4 GiB); Windows opens the pipe at identification level (M9).
- A plugin page's `%` before a non-ASCII character no longer panics the
  protocol handler (L7).
- The Linux hotkeys helper is never looked up on PATH (I1).
- Every CI action is pinned to a commit (M13).
